Z||000029||rogergarrison||11-16-2001||07:36 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnF:<BR><B>I'm with johnt671 on this one.<P>About $400/yr for complete coverage liability/collision ($200 ded)/comprehensive ($50 ded), and, incidentally, road tow service to $80.00/event.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>same here. I got some quotes for collector type car insurance, but I didnt like the idea of them telling me when i can drive my car. I drive hundreds of miles just for the fun of it, and everywhere except places I have to park beside other ppl (malls, theaters,etc)<P><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 11-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000030||Oreif||11-16-2001||08:16 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>  same here. I got some quotes for collector type car insurance, but I didnt like the idea of them telling me when i can drive my car. I drive hundreds of miles just for the fun of it, and everywhere except places I have to park beside other ppl (malls, theaters,etc)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thru Nationwide, I have no restrictions on when I can drive it. I store it over the winter by my choice. The "pleasure" part just means it's not my daily driver (with 2 kids that need to be dropped off at a sitter everyday I need more than 2-seats) and the "collector" part is to insure it at it's appraised value and exempt me from emission testing.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-16-2001).]||||reg||1
